desc:Corpus v2.3.3 - Repeat to MIDI
tags:instrument sampler granular synthesis ui
// #GFX_RESIZE: responsive
// #FILE: Corpus sources {Slot 0: use Open Multiple, as in Sample v71. A single long file is valid.}
filename:0,sample.wav
in_pin:none
out_pin:Left
out_pin:Right
options:maxmem=25165824 gfx_hz=30
// @za:gfx_sync_policy EXPLICIT
// @za:gfx_sync_mem 49152 16384 DSP_TO_GFX
// Corpus v0.7.0: combined representation, walk, envelope, mutation, branching,
// and exploration prototype. Requires Sample v71's EXTENDED sample-pool host.
// Requires this repository's structured-task AOT runtime; not stock REAPER JSFX.
// Loader and analysis scaffolding derived from Corpus v0.1.2 / Sample v71.
// DSP owns corpus, analysis, scheduler, history and voices. GFX reads ONLY the
// bounded explicit snapshot and writes acknowledged slider24 command packets.
// Audio stays in the immutable host pool. Never adopt while voices/events exist.
// Roles are four independent fuzzy eligibilities, NEVER exclusive retrieval bins.
// Feature labels are acoustic PROXIES, not learned semantic/material recognition.
// The map is a user-selected two-descriptor projection, not a neural embedding.
// Existing slider slots are preserved; role filtering is now fuzzy eligibility.
// v0.9.3: decoupled analysis/audio clocks, active-run playback spans, audible-hole diagnostics.
// v1.9.8: Texture-aware native spectral pitch, prepared per-voice engines and source-lookahead latency compensation.
// v1.9.6: host-backed Original/Mono source mode and automatic recovery from failed/cancelled preparation tasks.
// v1.9.5: host-backed grain Shape/Softness/Balance and per-walker overlap leveling.
// v1.9.1: stage-specific load progress, prompt loader polling and snapshot-stall status.
// v1.7.0: optional EC Focus adds class-local Essence + PC1/PC2/PC3 refinement without changing broad class discovery.
// v1.7.1: explicit axis buttons, audible dot scrubbing, preview-vs-apply focus ranges, and immediate focused audition.
// v1.8.0: reverts the experimental structural-interpretation branch and adds bounded transient diffusion only.
// v1.8.1: Transient Diffusion is host-backed/automatable on slider45; map stratum paging moved to private UI state.
// v1.5.1: child walkers own independent Micro lineages; newer controls support right-click reset.
// v1.5.0: performance-first Explore and bounded 0..12 child cloud with gap-fill action.
// v1.4.0: unified 51-axis descriptor registry, corpus-derived axes, variable Auto Micro segmentation, and Structure re-synthesis audition.
// v1.4.1: X/Y descriptor selection uses an in-plugin scrollable picker instead of an OS-sized menu.
// Slots 22/23 now hold quiet detection and source matching. Slot IDs otherwise stable.
// New defaults are for fresh instances. Saved explicit choices are not overwritten.
// #HELP: Load files in slot 0, wait for INDEX READY, click grains/vertices to hear them.
// #HELP: MIDI notes launch the same continuous walker in One-shot or Gated mode.
// #HELP: A/D/R are milliseconds; known windows proportionally fit A+D+R when needed.
// #HELP: Sustain is gain. Stability is the separate identity-leash parameter.
// #HELP: Draw a map path to guide selected descriptor axes through an event.
// #HELP: Click map point = audition, Shift = anchor, Ctrl+drag = focus, Draw = path.
// #HELP: Structure: click Meso/Macro = re-synthesize with the current engine; Shift+click = original source region; Ctrl+click = pending exclusion.
// #HELP: EC Focus is an optional second-stage Meso refinement. Essence measures class-defining direction vs corpus background; PC1/PC2/PC3 measure within-class variation. Click/drag member dots to audition originals, Shift-click a dot to re-synthesize it, and drag the lower range strip to preview/retain a slice. FOCUS ON applies that slice to generation; broad EC membership is never destroyed.
// #HELP: Child walkers share the structural trajectory but own independent Micro lineages; Follow is not a grain-for-grain clone.
// #HELP: Trajectories has its own workspace: twelve saved lanes, eight draggable time handles or freehand Draw, shape presets, per-lane Undo, reverse/invert, mute/solo/duplicate, and requested-versus-actual traces. Target seeks proximity; Ceiling/Maximum and Floor/Minimum penalize only violations. Global Influence and lane Strength are absolute weights; zero bypass removes both scoring and trajectory candidates. Event fits known durations; held notes repeat over Seconds. Once holds its end, Repeat restarts, Bounce travels forward and back. Start Offset changes phase. Curves and lane metadata use float-exact host parameters; no shared-runtime behavior is changed.
// #HELP: Descriptor lanes use cached 54-axis evidence and bounded successor lookahead; no FFT or corpus analysis runs from playback.
// #HELP: Transient Diffusion is a separate post-selection renderer and a real host parameter (slider45), so copy/paste, presets and automation use normal JSFX parameter state. Zero is exact bypass. Grain uses eight windowed unity-speed grains with identical L/R timing; high amounts create a diffuse cloud without adding stereo width. Classic retains the former all-pass renderer. Selection is unchanged, and event deadlines still cap the result.
// #HELP: Grain Tame attenuates overly loud fragments before they are mixed: a cached RMS/peak estimate sets a fixed gain per new voice, and a stereo-linked gentle soft peak guard catches missed spikes. No quiet-grain makeup, pumping envelope or live PCM analysis is used. Zero bypasses exactly; one gives full taming. Source auditions stay original and REPEAT preserves the recorded gain/guard.
// #HELP: Pitch behavior selects Tape (speed/duration pitching) or Coherent (texture-aware spectral resynthesis at the original excerpt timing). Coherent transposes the low/mid body while progressively shifting upper noisy frequencies less. Cached tonal confidence sets the crossover; attacks favor texture retention. Stereo phase relationships are linked. Native engines are prepared before playback; bounded lookahead stays within the chosen excerpt, avoiding MIDI latency. Zero pitch bypasses exactly and very short spans retain Tape. REPEAT captures pitch, texture confidence and duration. This is a perceptual effect: upper frequencies do not all transpose by the full requested interval.
// #HELP: Source channels at the top selects Original or Mono for every loaded recording. Mono averages L/R before grain panning, without editing files. Playback glides to the new mode; analysis rebuilds automatically when current events finish. Child spread can still create a stereo cloud from mono sources.
// #HELP: Grain Shape selects Original, Rounded, or Soft rise; Softness broadens each grain's fades. Overlap Level uses Energy for noise-like textures or Amplitude for correlated repeats; Off restores the original summation. Explore exposes these three controls together. Optional Grain Balance moves the peak later/earlier. These are host parameters, applied to future grains and captured by REPEAT. Original + Off preserves the old renderer. Source auditions remain unshaped.
// #HELP: ADSR includes independent Attack, Decay and Release curves, from Fast through Linear to Slow, with an envelope preview. Curves are snapshotted per event and restored by REPEAT; zero preserves the former linear envelope. Sustain remains a level. Right-click a curve to reset it to Linear.
// #HELP: Duration CC ADSR defaults to Relative: inherited A/D/R proportions scale from the One-shot window to the incoming duration. Absolute retains milliseconds; Hub A/R percentages override either mode. Fit includes release in the window; Free/Tail allow the tail after it. Ordinary note timing is unchanged.
// #HELP: Amplitude can use curved ADSR or a custom smooth freehand MSEG curve. Fixed one-shots traverse the whole curve; Gated/Natural hold at the sustain marker then traverse the release segment.
// #HELP: Right-click resets both ordinary and newer cloud/coherence controls to their documented defaults.
// #HELP: Explore is the performance surface: child cloud, lifecycle, ADSR, overlap/coherence and descriptor map are reachable without changing pages.
// #HELP: Up to 12 non-recursive child walkers can act as Follow, Resonance, Debris, Contrast, Shadow, Body bed (formerly Fill-gaps), or Mixed companions. Count, mode, density and timing spread are real saved/automatable host parameters 76-79; Level, Similarity and Width retain their existing parameters. Child Level is total-cloud intent and is energy-compensated as count rises.
// #HELP: Grain detection is visible in the main header. Auto preserves the existing default; Aggressive favors short units and plays their exact spans. Coherent is opt-in: sustained pauses and persistent acoustic changes close units, with no fixed duration limit by default. Sensitivity and an optional seconds limit are saved host parameters. Requires Micro=Auto. Coherent playback uses the indexed region itself, bypasses Auto excerpt/event-fraction caps, uses short edge fades and near-end crossfades; event deadlines, stops, pruning, source bounds and Macro REST remain authoritative. Acoustic continuity is not sentence/semantic recognition. Longer passages respond less quickly to trajectories. Analysis rebuilds when current events finish.
// #HELP: All panes scroll. Small windows use tabs; no minimum-size blocker.
// #HELP: Sample Hub CC118/119 v1 packets: Play/Retrigger/Continue/Choke/End supported.
// #HELP: Unsupported modifier packets are rejected and counted, not misinterpreted.
// #HELP: REPEAT uses a completed recorded plan; overflow/continued/forced plans are disabled.
// #HELP: Live controls affect future selections; replay uses recorded decisions.
// #HELP: Analysis rebuilds automatically after source/settings changes; active audio finishes first.
// #HELP: Micro/Meso boundaries retarget future selections; they never truncate sounding audio.
// #HELP: Only event deadlines, explicit stops/source ends and Macro REST may terminate active audio.
// #HELP: Inspector distinguishes scheduler gaps, source holes and final audible holes.
// #HELP: Source matching is capped at +24 dB. Low-salience material stays playable; only Macro may schedule structural REST.
// #HELP: Draw commits on mouse-up. Locks/scope remain authoritative; target error is visible.
